@reactions gift
// Writer-commons, reactions. The day after you gave someone a gift (social's cue gift.<tag>, one day; .you, @me: the
// person who got it). The thank-you on the day is the `gift` line kind; this is the next day's mention.

? cue:gift.tea.you@me
- I've had three cups of that tea already. Don't tell anyone. They'll want some.   #funny
- That tea you gave me. Perfect for the night shift. Or any shift. {thanks}.
? cue:gift.sweet.you@me
- The biscuits are gone. All of them. I regret nothing.   #funny
- I shared your biscuits. Well, one. The rest I guarded. {thanks}.   #funny
? cue:gift.star.you@me
- I put the star chart up by my bunk. I look at it every night.   #warm
? cue:gift.plant.you@me
- The plant's doing well. I've named it. Not Gerald. Well. Gerald.   #funny
- Your little plant's put out a new leaf. I was ridiculously pleased.   #warm
? cue:gift.book.you@me
- I stayed up reading the book you gave me. Chapter nine. Don't tell me anything.
? cue:gift.garden.you@me
- Those herbs made my dinner. Brennan was jealous. Brennan's never jealous.   #funny
? cue:gift.made.you@me
- That thing you made me is on my shelf. Made in the machine shop! I show everyone.   #warm
? cue:gift.music.you@me
- I've played the music you gave me four times. Five. It's very good.
? cue:gift.game.you@me
- That puzzle! I solved it at two in the morning and woke half the bunk shouting.   #funny
? cue:gift.you@me tier>=friend
- Still thinking about that present. You didn't have to. I'm glad you did.   #warm

? cue:gift.you !cue:gift.you@me tier>=acquaintance
- I hear you've been giving presents. Very kind. Very suspicious.   #funny
- Someone's walking round very pleased with a gift. I heard it was from you.
